        "category": null,
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Two or more creatures enter the haunt's area</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> Each creature sees the forms of nearby creatures shift and change, appearing to transform into fiendish or aberrant beings with a thirst for blood. Each creature in the area must attempt a @Check[will|dc:30] save. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature sees through the illusions entirely and is temporarily immune to the haunt's routine for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the strange images.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature believes the illusions to be true; if they become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.yblD8fOR1J8rDwEQ]{Confused} by the haunt's routine, they can't attempt flat checks to end the confused condition when they take damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is left with a lingering suspicion of others and can't benefit from Aid reactions for 24 hours.</p>",
